2. Detection: only explicitly launched local repository/worktree roots, no home-wide watch and no remote-host fiction. notify callback queues bounded normalized paths only; bounded IO jobs hash regular files without following symlinks or reading file bodies into events. Capture created/modified/deleted and paired renames with before/after digests; uncertain rename stays delete+create. Existing authenticated W2.3 Write/Edit hook paths give reported attribution; filesystem timing gives inferred attribution only. Unknown hook shapes never become certainty. Parse existing git HEAD/ref changes and existing Bboxy-Seat trailers as metadata, without invoking shell text or installing hooks.
